    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007-sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "4 Subsection 21(2)",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007#sch-1-sec-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral eligibility\n\n(2) A person is eligible to become an Australian citizen if the Minister\nis satisfied that the person:\n\n(a) is aged 18 or over at the time the person made the\napplication; and\n\n(b) is a permanent resident at that time; and\n\n(c) satisfies the residence requirement (see section 22), or has\ncompleted relevant defence service (see section 23), at that\ntime; and\n\n(d) understands the nature of an application under subsection (1);\nand\n\n(e) possesses a basic knowledge of the English language; and\n\n(f) has an adequate knowledge of Australia and of the\nresponsibilities and privileges of Australian citizenship; and\n\n(g) is likely to reside, or to continue to reside, in Australia or to\nmaintain a close and continuing association with Australia if\nthe application were to be approved; and\n\n(h) is of good character at the time of the Minister’s decision on\nthe application.\n\n(2A) Paragraphs (2)(d), (e) and (f) are taken to be satisfied if and only if\nthe Minister is satisfied that the person has, before making the\napplication:\n\n(a) sat a test approved in a determination under section 23A; and\n\n(b) successfully completed that test (worked out in accordance\nwith that determination).",
      "skos:definition": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral eligibility\n\n(2) A person is eligible to become an Australian citizen if the Minister\nis satisfied that the person:\n\n(a) is aged 18 or over at the time the person made the\napplication; and\n\n(b) is a permanent resident at that time; and\n\n(c) satisfies the residence requirement (see section 22), or has\ncompleted relevant defence service (see section 23), at that\ntime; and\n\n(d) understands the nature of an application under subsection (1);\nand\n\n(e) possesses a basic knowledge of the English language; and\n\n(f) has an adequate knowledge of Australia and of the\nresponsibilities and privileges of Australian citizenship; and\n\n(g) is likely to reside, or to continue to reside, in Australia or to\nmaintain a close and continuing association with Australia if\nthe application were to be approved; and\n\n(h) is of good character at the time of the Minister’s decision on\nthe application.\n\n(2A) Paragraphs (2)(d), (e) and (f) are taken to be satisfied if and only if\nthe Minister is satisfied that the person has, before making the\napplication:\n\n(a) sat a test approved in a determination under section 23A; and\n\n(b) successfully completed that test (worked out in accordance\nwith that determination).",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007-sch-1-sec-4-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007-sch-1-sec-4-ss-2a"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a998aeb4e7da6d659bab77c464e84f3266fab8319712f877b7b1b3a812ad69cd"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007#sch-1-sec-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "4 Subsection 21(2)",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 8,
      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\nGeneral eligibility\n\n(2) A person is eligible to become an Australian citizen if the Minister\nis satisfied that the person:\n\n(a) is aged 18 or over at the time the person made the\napplication; and\n\n(b) is a permanent resident at that time; and\n\n(c) satisfies the residence requirement (see section 22), or has\ncompleted relevant defence service (see section 23), at that\ntime; and\n\n(d) understands the nature of an application under subsection (1);\nand\n\n(e) possesses a basic knowledge of the English language; and\n\n(f) has an adequate knowledge of Australia and of the\nresponsibilities and privileges of Australian citizenship; and\n\n(g) is likely to reside, or to continue to reside, in Australia or to\nmaintain a close and continuing association with Australia if\nthe application were to be approved; and\n\n(h) is of good character at the time of the Minister’s decision on\nthe application.\n\n(2A) Paragraphs (2)(d), (e) and (f) are taken to be satisfied if and only if\nthe Minister is satisfied that the person has, before making the\napplication:\n\n(a) sat a test approved in a determination under section 23A; and\n\n(b) successfully completed that test (worked out in accordance\nwith that determination)."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007-sch-1-sec-4-ss-2",
