    {
      "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007-sch-1-sec-23a",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "23A Citizenship test",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007#sch-1-sec-23a"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007.pdf, p.8",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Minister must, by written determination, approve a test for the\npurposes of subsection 21(2A) (about general eligibility for\ncitizenship).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNote:\nThe test must be related to the eligibility criteria referred to in\nparagraphs 21(2)(d), (e) and (f).\nSuccessful completion of the test\n\n(2) A determination under subsection (1) must specify what amounts\nto successful completion of the test.\nEligibility criteria for sitting the test\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (1) may set out the eligibility\ncriteria a person must satisfy to be able to sit the test.\nNote:\nThe eligibility criteria for sitting the test cannot be inconsistent with\nthis Act and in particular subsection 21(2) (about the general\neligibility criteria for becoming an Australian citizen).\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the determination may provide\nthat a person is not eligible to sit the test unless the person is a\npermanent resident and the Minister is satisfied of the identity of\nthe person.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not limit subsection (3).\nOther matters\n\n(6) A determination under subsection (1) may cover any other matter\nrelated to the test the Minister thinks appropriate.\nDetermination not a legislative instrument\n\n(7) A determination made under subsection (1) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Minister must, by written determination, approve a test for the\npurposes of subsection 21(2A) (about general eligibility for\ncitizenship).\n\nAmendments  Schedule 1\n\nNote:\nThe test must be related to the eligibility criteria referred to in\nparagraphs 21(2)(d), (e) and (f).\nSuccessful completion of the test\n\n(2) A determination under subsection (1) must specify what amounts\nto successful completion of the test.\nEligibility criteria for sitting the test\n\n(3) A determination under subsection (1) may set out the eligibility\ncriteria a person must satisfy to be able to sit the test.\nNote:\nThe eligibility criteria for sitting the test cannot be inconsistent with\nthis Act and in particular subsection 21(2) (about the general\neligibility criteria for becoming an Australian citizen).\n\n(4) For the purposes of subsection (3), the determination may provide\nthat a person is not eligible to sit the test unless the person is a\npermanent resident and the Minister is satisfied of the identity of\nthe person.\n\n(5) Subsection (4) does not limit subsection (3).\nOther matters\n\n(6) A determination under subsection (1) may cover any other matter\nrelated to the test the Minister thinks appropriate.\nDetermination not a legislative instrument\n\n(7) A determination made under subsection (1) is not a legislative\ninstrument.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:australian-citizenship-amendment-citizenship-testing-act-2007-sch-1-sec-23a-ss-1"
        },
